│ Location 1:                                                        │
│ File: django/forms/widgets.py                                      │
│ Class: Widget                                                      │
│ Method: render                                                     │
│ Intended behavior:                                                 │
│ The render method generates the HTML for the widget by calling     │
│ render_ methods for each media type (e.g., render_text,            │
│ render_html, etc.). This is the core logic for rendering the       │
│ widget's HTML output.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ Bug location:                                                      │
│ The issue lies in the render method of the Widget class,           │
│ specifically the part where it iterates over MEDIA_TYPES to call   │
│ render_ methods. The current implementation includes a default     │
│ blank option when the field is required (i.e., blank=False is set  │
│ on the model).                                                     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            🛠 Root Cause                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The RadioSelect widget (a subclass of ChoiceWidget) is rendering a │
│ blank option (---------) when blank=False is set on the model      │
│ field. This is because the render method of the Widget class       │
│ includes a default option for required fields, which is not        │
│ desired.                                                           │
│                                                                    │
│ What the code does:                                                │
│ The render method uses getattr(self, 'render_' + name)() for each  │
│ MEDIA_TYPE, which may include a default option for required        │
│ fields. When blank=False is set, the widget incorrectly adds a     │
│ blank option.                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│ Relationship to the bug:                                           │
│ The render method in the Widget class is responsible for           │
│ generating the HTML for the widget. The blank option is part of    │
│ the default rendering logic, which is not aligned with the         │
│ intended behavior when blank=False is specified.                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                        🛠 Intended Behavior                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is that the RadioSelect widget should not    │
│ render a blank option when the field is required (i.e.,            │
│ blank=False is set on the model). The blank option is only         │
│ displayed when the field is optional (blank=True), which is the    │
│ expected behavior for select widgets.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    ✅ Summary of Bug Locations                     │
