│ Location 2:                                                        │
│ File: django/forms/widgets.py                                      │
│ Class: RadioSelect                                                 │
│ Method: render()                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Intended Behavior:                                                 │
│ The render() method should exclude the blank option when           │
│ blank=False is set on the model field. The blank option is         │
│ typically added in the render() method, but the render_options()   │
│ method is responsible for generating individual radio options.     │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                         🛠️ Summary of Fixes                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The bug lies in the render() method of RadioSelect (a subclass of  │
│ ChoiceWidget). The blank option is added regardless of the         │
│ blank=False setting. To fix this:                                  │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Modify the render() method to exclude the blank option when     │
│    blank=False is set.                                             │
│  2 Ensure the render_options() method does not generate the blank  │
│    option in this context.                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ This aligns with the intended behavior of the widget, which should │
│ not display a blank option when it is not allowed.                 │
